 "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3184118/new-delete-malloc-free",
 "body_html": "<p>This question was asked to me in an interview:</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>In  C++,</p>\n  \n  <ol>\n  <li>what if we allocate memory using <code>malloc</code> and use <code>delete</code> to free that allocated memory?</li>\n  <li>what if we allocate the memory using <code>new</code> and free it using <code>free</code>?</li>\n  </ol>\n  \n  <p>What are the problems that we would face if the above things are used in the code?</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>My answer was there is no difference. Was I right in saying so?</p>\n",
 "passes": [
  "main"
 ],
 "data_source": "so_main_cached (2026-10-05 collection)",
 "in_main_retained_480": true,
 "in_main_nonNA_coded_346": false,
